# host-text-normalised-to-nfc: each value is read as the code points written,
# built through the Host's text constructor, which normalises it to NFC, and
# encoded. The encoded text is written as raw UTF-8, since the Value Encoding
# escapes only `"`, `\` and U+0000 to U+001F.
# The bytes were written by hand from chapter 9, and the TS Core reproduces
# them exactly.
#
# "e" then U+0301 COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT composes to U+00E9.
"e" & fromCodePoint(769) => "é"
# U+212B ANGSTROM SIGN is a singleton, and becomes U+00C5.
fromCodePoint(8491) => "Å"
# A mark with nothing to compose with stays as it is.
fromCodePoint(769) => "́"
# Inside a list and a map key, too.
["e" & fromCodePoint(769)] => ["é"]
{"e" & fromCodePoint(769): 1} => {"é":1}
